Package: fivenumMeta
Type: Package
Title: Five-Number Summaries Based Estimation and Inference in Meta-Analysis
Version: 0.1.0
Date: 2026-10-17
Authors@R: c(
    person("Zheyang", "Wu", email = "zheyangwu@wpi.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
    )
Description: Tools for meta-analyses of studies that report a median with quartiles
    or extremes (a five-number summary or part of it) instead of the sample
    mean and sample standard deviation (SD). The current version focuses on
    calculating the precision of the mean and standard deviation imputed
    from such a summary, under normality. It includes the standard deviation
    factors (SDF) and the inflation factors (IF) of these imputed estimators,
    exactly, for the best linear unbiased estimators and for the shortcut
    estimators of Wan, Luo and Shi. It also provides closed-form shortcut
    formulas for these factors. Supporting functions are included to
    calculate the imputed mean and SD of a study with their plug-in standard
    errors, and to pool the studies under the naive and the exact standard
    errors, for practical meta-analysis. The methods are described by Wu, Shi
    and Tong (2026) in 'Precision of the imputed mean and standard deviation
    from a five-number summary' (manuscript). The moments of the normal order
    statistics come from the 'osmoments' package, described by Wu and Tong
    (2026) in 'osmoments: Exact Means, Variances and Covariances of Order
    Statistics in R' (manuscript).
